      "writtenOn": "2025-01-20T13:24:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it okay to repurpose `ART_USE_GENERATIONAL_CC` to mean generational CMC? Will it cause confusions? Personally, I don\u0027t have an opinion on this. I just wonder other ART folks\u0027 opinion, especially those who work on the runtime.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 79,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 79,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "668385ebd4654216f1cdae8ef58acb3ba15f9f4a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7ba4dfcd_3ce74b4c",
        "filename": "build/art.go",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1052644
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-20T18:53:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I presume reusing the `ART_USE_GENERATIONAL_CC` environment variable / macro is meant to leverage existing continuous integration configurations (e.g. on LUCI and Golem), but I agree this is confusing. I\u0027d also recommend introducing a new unambiguous name here (e.g. `ART_USE_GENERATIONAL_GC`).\n\nWe should also consider moving away from using `ART_USE_READ_BARRIER` to mean \"CC collector vs other collector\" as this is confusing, e.g. by generalising the use of an explicit \"GC type\" environment variable / macro instead – but this is a bit orthogonal to this CL, so this would be fine to do in a separate CL.",
      "parentUuid": "f4fa23e8_f9faf924",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 79,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 79,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "668385ebd4654216f1cdae8ef58acb3ba15f9f4a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4cd0c01e_cfae7150",
        "filename": "build/art.go",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1258954
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T06:46:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Exactly as Roland said, The only reason I\u0027m kind of forced to keep `ART_USE_GENERATIONAL_CC` and `-Xgc:generational_cc` is so that we don\u0027t break all the test setup that we have. That\u0027s why you\u0027ll notice wherever I could, I replaced `cc/CC` with `gc/GC`.\n\nI\u0027m introducing new `ART_USE_GENERATIONAL_GC` and `-Xgc:generational_gc`, but for backward compatibility, will have to keep the older ones. PTAL.",
      "parentUuid": "7ba4dfcd_3ce74b4c",
