      "side": 1,
      "message": "Discussed with Lokesh offline. There is a build failure due to RW flags unsupported for the [libcore\u0027s usage with `sdk_version: \"none\"`](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:libcore/JavaLibrary.bp;l\u003d1123;drc\u003d47fea5deb5e320dd6a7a5b532e5dbea7b9be22c0). I suggested to move this flag back to RO because:\n\n1. Lokesh\u0027s intention is to advance the flag quickly to make it to Beta 3. That means we won\u0027t stay in the Trunkfood Partial stage for long for A/B testing, so there isn\u0027t much value in using an RW flag.\n2. Lokesh said performance numbers from dogfood population are not representive, which defeats the value of using an RW flag too.",
