      "writtenOn": "2025-01-20T18:53:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Lokesh, IIUC you are reusing [the logic in `app_process` / Zygote which is reading the `runtime_native_boot/enable_generational_cc` \"legacy\" P/H flag and passing it to the runtime](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/core/jni/AndroidRuntime.cpp;l\u003d922-932;drc\u003d3366756f141c921f7ef5210e6be34877b7d4dc3f) here. Ideally, we should try and move away from this approach, as it relies on code living in the non-Mainline-updatable platform.\n\nTo \"dynamically\" control the generational behaviour of the new GC, I think we should introduce a new P/H flag (and read it in ART rather than in `app_process`), instead of piggingbacking on `runtime_native_boot/enable_generational_cc`. As discussed last week, we should eventually have three P/H flags to control 1. the GC type, 2. whether the GC is generational, and 3. whether the MOVE ioctl should be used (when applicable).",
      "parentUuid": "66f991ff_32e6b151",
      "range": {
