      "writtenOn": "2025-01-22T14:12:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry if my comment was not clear.\n\nWhat I meant is that `art::gc::collector::YoungMarkCompact::gc_time_histogram_` (and similar fields inherited from `art::gc::collector::GarbageCollector`) won\u0027t be used in practice, given that `art::gc::collector::YoungMarkCompact` delegates everything to an instance of `art::gc::collector::MarkCompact` (which does not know about the `art::gc::collector::YoungMarkCompact` instance). (Actually I\u0027d recommend to initialise them to `nullptr` to catch unintended uses early).\n\nI think you need to assign `art::gc::collector::MarkCompact::gc_time_histogram_` and related fields to the right metric field every time a collection starts in `art::gc::collector::MarkCompact::RunPhases`, depending on the collection type.",
